CloudBurrow patch 6 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1138); needs patches 0004 and 0005.

The bug: a GEOGRAPHY given as WKT text in a streamed row, a load or a
query's rows kept its numbers as written, POINT(1.0 2), where BigQuery
writes each coordinate in its shortest form, POINT(1 2) (as the engine's
own ST_ASTEXT already does, googlesqlite patch 12). Measured on the patched
emulator built natively: insertAll of POINT(1.0 2) read back POINT(1.0 2).
bigQueryWKTValue (internal/contentdata/geography.go, patch 0004) now also
writes each number with strconv.FormatFloat(f, 'f', -1, 64).

